<title>TUNISIA: Tunisian Treasury raises 31 mln dinars at auction.</title>
<headline>Tunisian Treasury raises 31 mln dinars at auction.</headline>
<dateline>TUNIS 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tunisian Treasury on Tuesday said it sold 31 million dinars of two-year notes at its weekly auction on Sept 10, repaying maturing paper totalling 14.6 million dinars.</p>
<p>The issue raised the following amounts (in million of Tunisian dinars):</p>
<p>		Term			  Yield	    Amount</p>
<p>					     (pct)</p>
<p>-Two-year payable at maturity</p>
<p>					     9.0625	     2</p>
<p>-Two-year payable in equal</p>
<p>annual tranches</p>
<p>					    9.0000	     13.5</p>
<p>					    9.0625	     1.5</p>
<p>					    9.1250	     13</p>
<p>-Three-year payable at maturity   9.1250	     1</p>
<p>Banks bidded for 60 million dinars for two, three, four and five-year notes at between 9.000 and 9.5 percent.  ($=0.96 dinar)</p>
</text>
